Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.42,0:00:04.36,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Send them one by one?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.36,0:00:07.22,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,Yes. Sophia's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.22,0:00:10.89,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,She told us to send in the \Ntransmogrified phantoms one by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.23,0:00:14.94,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,What the hell is she thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.94,0:00:19.29,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,That's essentially begging for\Nthem to be defeated individually.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.29,0:00:21.80,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,In the end, she's only a scientist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.80,0:00:24.63,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,She doesn't know what a \Nreal battle is all about!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.38,0:00:28.25,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Call her here immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.25,0:00:31.10,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,She went out to check the defense systems,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.10,0:00:34.36,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,and she's not answering her \NSounding Stone either.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.36,0:00:35.56,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.56,0:00:37.52,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,We're up against Thousand Tricks here!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.52,0:00:39.94,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,We can take all the precautions we want,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.94,0:00:43.75,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,but if the leader is incompetent, \Nwe can even lose this easy fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.18,0:00:48.48,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,Flick, even though our mentor said \Nthat he gives her full authority,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.48,0:00:50.60,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,winning is what is crucial here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.31,0:00:53.54,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.81,0:00:56.86,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,At this rate, she will embarrass our mentor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.29,0:00:59.80,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Let all the phantoms loose!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.80,0:01:01.40,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,We'll crush them in one go!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.40,0:01:02.04,Default,Both,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.59,0:01:04.39,Internal,Flick(M),0,0,0,,Sophia Black.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.39,0:01:08.39,Internal,Flick(M),0,0,0,,I'll show you how to do battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.74,0:01:16.06,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,So these are the guys who \Nmade that slime-like thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.06,0:01:19.60,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,It only took a single injection\Nto create such a monster, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.30,0:01:24.30,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Let us get right to the point.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.30,0:01:27.64,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Your boss is the Master of Mages, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.18,0:01:30.92,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,My name is Sitri Smart.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.92,0:01:35.48,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,We can guarantee your safety, so please \Ntell us where he can be found.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.82,0:01:37.94,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,A-As if we'd tell you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.94,0:01:40.21,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,We'll happily give our lives for our mentor!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.09,0:01:42.14,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.14,0:01:44.34,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,You're Noctus Cochlear's disciples.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.37,0:01:50.46,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I'll have you know that I've been \Nfollowing the Akashic Tower for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.46,0:01:52.82,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I know about you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.82,0:01:55.22,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I don't want to have to \Nuse uncivilized measures.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.58,0:01:57.98,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Where is Noctus Cochlear?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.81,0:02:02.23,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.52,0:02:05.58,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Why don't I use this, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.58,0:02:08.18,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,This potion should \Nloosen your tongue a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.18,0:02:09.86,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,Stop right there, Sitri Smart.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.86,0:02:12.85,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,Isn't that an illegal potion?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.85,0:02:16.54,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,It can muddle someone's consciousness, \Nforce a confession, or erase memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.54,0:02:19.99,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,It can also potentially be used\Nfor brainwashing. It's very dangerous!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.99,0:02:23.29,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you concocted this yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.31,0:02:27.25,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,That's irrelevant. If we don't hurry, \NNoctus Cochlear will get away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.25,0:02:28.63,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,This is for justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.50,0:02:31.53,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Easy, Adoria.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.53,0:02:32.51,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Sitri.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.90,0:02:35.20,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,I understand where you're coming from,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.20,0:02:38.30,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,but you can't just do whatever\Nyou want to prisoners.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.12,0:02:41.25,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,We're not criminals.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.46,0:02:44.40,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,You, of all people, should \Nunderstand that the most.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.77,0:02:46.54,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.54,0:02:48.06,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It was a joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.06,0:02:50.66,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,This really is just colored water.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.86,0:02:59.79,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,See? Nothing happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.36,0:03:02.16,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.16,0:03:06.15,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I mean, I do have a resistance \Nagainst colored water.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.60,0:03:07.83,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,More importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.30,0:03:10.58,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,it seems we've run out of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.48,0:03:41.10,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,"Perfect Play."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.10,0:03:43.56,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,This isn't your ordinary water pistol.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.56,0:03:46.50,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It's a relic given to me \Nby someone important.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.49,0:03:49.50,EpTitle,Title,0,0,0,,{\c&H00BAFF&\pos(320.52,100.623)}Episode 08
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.49,0:03:49.50,EpTitle,Title,0,0,0,,{\fs30\bord3\pos(322.143,238.714)\c&HD1D1D1&}I Want to Rush In When It's Over
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.74,0:03:48.94,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,"I Want to Rush In When It's Over."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.17,0:04:07.97,Show Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,700)\pos(324,269)\fscx95\fscy76}Let This Grieving Soul Retire
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.20,0:04:26.59,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,It's finally time!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.59,0:04:28.48,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,This is the end for you all!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.48,0:04:31.62,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,A bunch of useless hunters \Nstanding in the way of progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.62,0:04:33.48,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,Just die already!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.95,0:04:37.46,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,You were right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.46,0:04:39.27,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,It wasn't just that one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.27,0:04:40.73,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,So now what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.73,0:04:44.77,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,There are several types of magic \Nbarrier that these phantoms can have.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.77,0:04:51.45,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,We need to narrow down which element \Nworks on which area in order to break it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.45,0:04:53.77,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,You sound downright relaxed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.11,0:04:56.21,Default,Lyle,0,0,0,,It's faster than the previous one!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.21,0:04:57.78,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,The color's different, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.78,0:04:59.95,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,This means its base is likely different.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.95,0:05:03.31,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Those with shields, \Nplease take to the front line!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.31,0:05:04.14,Default,Lyle,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.14,0:05:07.93,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,This is necessary to determine the \Nforce field's output and direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.93,0:05:11.05,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Please let go as soon as contact \Nis made with the shield.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.05,0:05:12.58,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Otherwise, it could rip off your arm!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.20,0:05:14.67,Default,Lyle,0,0,0,,Are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.67,0:05:17.33,Default,Lyle,0,0,0,,This really {\i1}is{\i0} just like he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.60,0:05:21.25,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Lyle!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.31,0:05:24.21,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Lyle!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.21,0:05:25.92,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Mages, please slow it down!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.93,0:05:30.72,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It's a revolving force field.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.72,0:05:32.28,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It turns clockwise.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.28,0:05:33.89,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Varies by body part?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.89,0:05:36.37,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,If it blows you away with just one touch,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.37,0:05:38.69,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,melee fighters don't have a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.69,0:05:41.32,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,So it would do that to my axe, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.32,0:05:42.45,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,What are we going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.45,0:05:44.10,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Wait until it runs out of magic?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.10,0:05:45.08,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.08,0:05:48.41,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Considering its size and the \Namount of mana material it has,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.41,0:05:50.32,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,it could easily last another hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.55,0:05:52.66,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,What a huge pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.66,0:05:56.00,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Now I see why Krai wanted to send Ark here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.00,0:05:59.84,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,If we concentrate all our magical attacks \Non one spot and hit it multiple times,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.84,0:06:03.77,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,or if we can temporarily nullify \Npart of the magic barrier,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.77,0:06:05.33,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,we could get through.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.69,0:06:08.28,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,But that would require\Nan extremely high level of skill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.28,0:06:09.53,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,And with this current crew...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.53,0:06:10.81,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,The next one's coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.46,0:06:16.02,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,There's more?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.78,0:06:18.35,Default,Henrik,0,0,0,,Seriously, now?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.72,0:06:20.75,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Sitri, let's retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.75,0:06:22.41,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Our people are exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.41,0:06:24.40,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,We can't hold out any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.40,0:06:26.74,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Running away won't be easy, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.74,0:06:29.94,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Even if we call in the mages for \Nreinforcement, it might be too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.08,0:06:32.55,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.98,0:06:34.94,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I'm {\i1}so {\i0}done with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.94,0:06:38.49,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I never thought people this stupid \Nwould be in the Akashic Tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.49,0:06:39.43,Default,Both,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.43,0:06:41.25,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Mages, stop the magical attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.56,0:06:43.37,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Everyone, step back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.55,0:07:00.16,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,What is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.16,0:07:01.77,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It's just as I expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.77,0:07:04.30,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,They probably attacked the hunters
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.30,0:07:08.14,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,in order to replenish their depleting \Nlevels of mana material.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.73,0:07:12.17,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,And the thing here with even more \Nmana material than the hunters is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.17,0:07:13.98,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Now I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.98,0:07:17.28,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Phantoms are masses of mana material.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.30,0:07:45.06,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,The only word for this is "asinine."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.06,0:07:47.45,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Not sure if we're lucky or what.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.92,0:07:48.95,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,I can't believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.95,0:07:50.56,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,The fruit of our great research...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.89,0:07:53.54,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,The transmogrified phantoms\N have such a weakness?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.02,0:07:55.20,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.71,0:07:59.72,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,didn't they just send them \Nin one after another?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.61,0:08:03.83,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,I'm sick of your utter stupidity!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.86,0:08:08.96,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,I told you to treat Sophia's \Nwords as if they were my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.29,0:08:11.65,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,To make matters worse, \Nyou didn't realize your mistake
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.65,0:08:13.85,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,and used up all the\Ntransmogrification potion!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.09,0:08:16.19,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,P-Please forgive us.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.19,0:08:19.61,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,We had no idea what had \Nhappened on the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.61,0:08:24.36,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Why did I choose not to send multiple \Ntransmogrified phantoms at once?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.36,0:08:27.00,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,If you think about it, it's obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.00,0:08:29.52,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,It's not that I lack experience in battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.52,0:08:32.12,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,nor am I giving out random directives.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.42,0:08:36.56,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Flick, you simply lack \Nwhat we call "imagination."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.28,0:08:39.61,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Oh, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.61,0:08:42.27,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,That was not the only weapon in our arsenal.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.27,0:08:44.60,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,What is our next move, Sophia?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.72,0:08:48.22,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,The situation has already changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.50,0:08:52.12,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Not only has Sitri Smart \Njoined the investigation party,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.12,0:08:56.13,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,but a former level 7 hunter, \NGark Welter, has as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.13,0:08:57.37,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.37,0:08:59.84,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,The Association's branch manager\Nhas come to the front lines?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.84,0:09:04.94,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Though he is long retired, he is \Nunmistakably one of the true heroes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.94,0:09:07.15,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Now that we have lost\Nthe transmogrification potions,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.15,0:09:09.27,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,our fight is going to be more difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.27,0:09:10.76,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Sophia, why you...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.76,0:09:12.34,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Stop it, Flick.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.34,0:09:13.52,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,You embarrass yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.52,0:09:15.96,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,F-Forgive me. I just...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.96,0:09:17.16,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,So what do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.51,0:09:18.94,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Do we retreat?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.46,0:09:20.17,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.75,0:09:23.41,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,We cannot walk away from this empty-handed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.04,0:09:28.42,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,That would influence your standing \Nwithin the Akashic Tower as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.42,0:09:31.87,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Most importantly, our side \Nhas had hostages taken.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.87,0:09:33.84,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,We don't know when they'll talk
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.84,0:09:35.54,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,How dare you, Sophia?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.54,0:09:39.60,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Those two are also seekers of truth who \Nhave sworn their loyalty to our mentor!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.60,0:09:41.73,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,They will reveal nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.73,0:09:44.75,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,I would also like for that to be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.18,0:09:48.08,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,But even without those \Ntwo spilling anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.08,0:09:51.80,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Sitri Smart will eventually \Nfind our headquarters.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.80,0:09:56.08,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Given that fact, it'll be a full-on battle \Nwhere we have to strike first to win.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.33,0:09:59.08,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Let us use the Malice \NEaters to overpower them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.58,0:10:03.76,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,We'll draw the survivors into our reach, \Nuse our trump cards, and destroy them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.76,0:10:07.09,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,If we kill them all, \Nthere will be no one left to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.12,0:10:09.92,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,An interesting idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.92,0:10:13.10,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,But the Malice Eaters are \Nstill only partially trained.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.45,0:10:17.22,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,For the best results, we'll need \Nsomeone to command them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.22,0:10:21.10,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Flick, it's finally time for you to shine.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.10,0:10:23.93,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,You're welcome to utilize \Nall of the creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.93,0:10:26.69,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,Please feel free to fully \Nunleash your power.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.11,0:10:31.59,Internal,Sophia,0,0,0,,I truly cannot imagine a mage of your \Nskill failing to succeed if you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.90,0:10:33.11,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.40,0:10:38.50,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Sir, I promise that I will \Nteach those hunters a lesson!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.80,0:10:53.47,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,Sitri Smart.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.82,0:10:55.63,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,A rare breed amongst hunters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.94,0:10:58.12,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,An alchemist, just like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.71,0:11:03.64,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,Fitting of her former second name, "The Prodigy,"
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.64,0:11:07.37,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,she was a person overflowing with \Noverwhelming talent and passion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.22,0:11:12.50,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,She was a born genius and a hard worker.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.27,0:11:15.14,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,In order to get closer to the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.49,0:11:18.91,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,she was willing to conduct any experiment, \Nno matter how dangerous or difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.36,0:11:22.14,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,She never gave up, no matter\Nhow daunting the situation,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.49,0:11:26.17,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,doing everything she could \Nwithin the confines of the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.73,0:11:30.41,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,She was so extraordinarily smart and pure
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.83,0:11:33.38,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,that I remember feeling \Nsomething akin to fear
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.38,0:11:35.93,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,and a tiny bit of jealousy next to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.47,0:11:39.78,Internal,Talia(M),0,0,0,,I could never become her.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.76,0:11:43.51,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Something on your mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.14,0:11:45.41,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,Sven...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.41,0:11:47.43,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,This afternoon was really intense.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.43,0:11:50.66,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,I never would've guessed that the \Nanti-slime stuff wouldn't work.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.66,0:11:52.71,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,I must have embarrassed you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.71,0:11:54.41,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,Oh, not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.41,0:11:58.26,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,The problem is that Krai always\Nleaves out vital information.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.26,0:12:02.56,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Like saying something is "slime-like" \Nwhen it's not a true slime at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.56,0:12:05.70,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,He really needs to rein in \Nthis Thousand Trials thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.62,0:12:08.07,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.07,0:12:11.53,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,So, I've been wondering this the entire time,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.53,0:12:14.20,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,but why do they keep staring at you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.20,0:12:17.96,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,Um, I don't really know.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.96,0:12:20.27,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Maybe because your hair stands out?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.27,0:12:23.37,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Well, anyway, if anything happens, \Nlet me know right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.37,0:12:24.48,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.22,0:12:29.64,Default,Talia,0,0,0,,What...?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.31,0:12:35.86,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Don't push yourself too hard, Sitri.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.99,0:12:38.32,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Gark.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.95,0:12:47.59,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,We may have mobilized a great many hunters,\Nbut this is still just an investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.59,0:12:49.59,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,If we're up against the Akashic Tower,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.59,0:12:52.07,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,this isn't something that the \NAssociation can handle by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.38,0:12:56.42,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Depending on their next moves,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.42,0:12:58.47,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,we should avoid overextending\Nand pull back for a—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.47,0:13:00.81,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I have figured out the rough \Nlocation of the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.81,0:13:01.99,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.50,0:13:06.70,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Well, anyway...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.70,0:13:10.01,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,By considering the flow of the ley lines, \Nthe concentration of mana material,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.01,0:13:13.86,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,the difference in altitude \Nand geological features,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.86,0:13:15.89,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,and where the slime-like things appeared,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.89,0:13:18.27,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,this cliff here seems to be \Na very likely place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.27,0:13:22.15,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,Such an in-depth analysis in such \Na short time, all by yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.15,0:13:23.65,Default,Adoria,0,0,0,,This is unbelievable.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.65,0:13:25.90,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Well, that's Sitri.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.90,0:13:29.13,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,So, did I get it right,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.13,0:13:31.78,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,disciples of Noctus Cochlear?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.78,0:13:35.38,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,Th-That's pure conjecture,\Nand it's completely wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.38,0:13:39.26,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,Totally off! That's not even\Nremotely where it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.26,0:13:41.43,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Looks like I guessed correctly, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.65,0:13:45.55,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It would even be possible to attack before \NNoctus Cochlear has a chance to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.82,0:13:49.02,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,If we've come this far,\Nwe should give it a shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.02,0:13:49.80,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.80,0:13:51.84,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,S-Stop it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.84,0:13:53.32,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,There's nothing there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.32,0:13:55.30,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,Our mentor isn't there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.30,0:13:57.37,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,We can't let them go over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.37,0:13:59.94,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,Sophia, hurry and untie our restraints!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.94,0:14:01.40,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Sophia?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.40,0:14:02.46,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.46,0:14:03.07,Default,Marietta,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.41,0:14:05.97,Default,Henrik,0,0,0,,It must be one of their friends nearby.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.97,0:14:07.32,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.63,0:14:10.69,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,If she'd just come out already,\Nthings would be easier.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.69,0:14:12.31,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Do you know her?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.31,0:14:13.15,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.55,0:14:17.48,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,She's Noctus Cochlear's \Ndisciple and my nemesis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.03,0:14:19.77,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Sophia Black.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.22,0:14:24.59,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,No matter how hard I look for her, \Nshe is as elusive as a shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.35,0:14:30.01,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,If we don't apprehend Noctus and Sophia, \Nthis kind of research will never end.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.68,0:14:35.60,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Simply put, those two together are\Nthe vilest and most evil mages of them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.60,0:14:38.23,Default,Tage,0,0,0,,As if Sophia would ever \Nlose to the likes of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.23,0:14:41.74,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,She may be an infuriating \Nwoman, but she's got skills!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.74,0:14:44.93,Default,Hos,0,0,0,,A level 2 failure like you stands no chance!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.93,0:14:49.73,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It is my ineptitude that has allowed \Nher to evade capture until now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.73,0:14:51.63,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,But I will not lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.63,0:14:56.88,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I swear on my honor that I will slam \Nher into the South Isteria prison!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.88,0:14:58.94,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Sitri... you...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.94,0:15:00.47,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It doesn't bother me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.30,0:15:05.32,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I am not blameless for that one case.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.78,0:15:10.75,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Krai, I love you!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.14,0:15:12.83,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I wanted to go even later,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.83,0:15:16.12,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,showing up when basically\Neverything was already done.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.31,0:15:18.90,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Let's hurry up and go!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.90,0:15:20.65,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Get moving before Si dies!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.65,0:15:22.01,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,She's not going to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.23,0:15:24.75,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,If anyone's dying, it's me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.75,0:15:26.94,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I couldn't charge any of my relics.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.94,0:15:29.52,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I don't have enough Safety Rings, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.52,0:15:31.53,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I'm in a pickle before we even start.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.53,0:15:34.71,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master, we're coming up \Non the White Wolf's Den.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.71,0:15:35.36,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.86,0:15:40.16,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I can't see a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.16,0:15:41.55,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Come on, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.55,0:15:44.28,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master, it's dark and dangerous, \Nso I was thinking I could...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.28,0:15:46.79,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,take your hand...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.79,0:15:48.05,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,How dare you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.28,0:15:52.07,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,It'll be a million light years before \Nyou're worthy to hold his hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.07,0:15:53.62,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Save the dreams for bedtime!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.62,0:15:55.32,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Actually, shut up and go to sleep!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.32,0:15:56.27,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Liz.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.27,0:15:58.76,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Light years are a measure \Nof distance, not time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.81,0:16:01.98,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Owl's Eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.81,0:16:06.59,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,This should do the trick for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.59,0:16:09.65,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I don't know how long this \Nrelic will hold up, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.95,0:16:12.00,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Just leave it to me, Krai!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.00,0:16:16.57,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,No matter who or what comes \Nat us, I'll kill 'em dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.57,0:16:18.99,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,You need to guard him, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.99,0:16:20.70,Top,Tino & Liz,0,0,0,,Y-Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.99,0:16:24.55,Top,Tino & Liz,0,0,0,,Not that I know what a useless \Nshit like you could even do!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.38,0:16:22.23,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,That reminds me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.23,0:16:26.21,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Sitri said something about the entire \Ninvestigation party getting wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.21,0:16:27.75,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I wonder if they're okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.23,0:16:33.72,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,I see. So Thousand Tricks isn't coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.72,0:16:38.27,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,The level 8 that you and \NObsidian Cross look up to...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.27,0:16:40.67,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,If only I had recognized \Nhis greatness earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.67,0:16:43.23,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,I wouldn't have ended up like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.23,0:16:47.92,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Krai is basically someone who was \Nborn to become a treasure hunter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.85,0:16:51.36,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I'm sure he'll eventually get to level 10.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.36,0:16:53.14,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,Level 10?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.14,0:16:55.58,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,Now I want to meet him even more.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.58,0:16:57.25,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,He must be really strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.25,0:16:58.79,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,He is.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.79,0:17:02.24,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,But strength is just one of many factors.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.56,0:17:08.84,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Even if Krai was hypothetically weaker than \Na sand rabbit in combat, it wouldn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.84,0:17:10.74,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,A sand rabbit?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.75,0:17:13.06,Default,Rabbit,0,0,0,,Bun bun?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.74,0:17:16.22,Default,Gein,0,0,0,,I don't think I quite understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.22,0:17:18.23,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,That's just how amazing he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.23,0:17:19.76,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Speaking of, Sitri.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.76,0:17:24.03,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,You didn't bring that magical creature \Nyou always have with you today?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.03,0:17:27.33,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Oh, if you mean Killiam, he's \Nundergoing maintenance right no—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.35,0:17:41.72,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,See that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.72,0:17:43.45,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,That's my high-level magic attack,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.45,0:17:45.39,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Calamity Thunder!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.39,0:17:50.61,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,You don't need that woman's defense \Nsystem as long as I'm around.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.20,0:17:57.68,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Looks like I used a bit too much mana,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.68,0:18:00.49,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,but my spells kill in one hit, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.49,0:18:04.94,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Killing the entire investigation \Nparty will make my mentor happy t—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.94,0:18:06.02,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,You bastard...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.02,0:18:07.44,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,So you're with the Akashic Tower!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.23,0:18:12.26,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,I guess you hunters are tough. \NI'll give you that much.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.26,0:18:13.81,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,But it's over now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.81,0:18:17.19,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,I'll bury you, along with the humiliation \Nthat woman inflicted upon me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.98,0:18:20.71,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I can't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.13,0:18:25.24,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,You used an area-of-effect \Nspell when we have hostages.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.81,0:18:30.11,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,I kind of knew I was no replacement for Krai.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.11,0:18:31.82,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Y-You!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.82,0:18:34.51,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Didn't you get hit by my Calamity Thunder?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.51,0:18:38.38,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Let me reply with a question: why do you \Nthink that spell would render me immobile?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.10,0:18:44.72,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Spells of that level aren't rare in the \Nhigh-level treasure vaults we frequent.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.72,0:18:46.24,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,Lies!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.24,0:18:49.98,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,You're saying my trump card—\Nthat my Calamity Thunder...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.98,0:18:52.23,Default,Flick,0,0,0,,is nothing special?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.02,0:18:57.50,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,It means that you simply lack \Nwhat we call "imagination."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.24,0:19:27.26,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,B-Branch Manager!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.24,0:19:29.85,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Sorry I took so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.66,0:19:33.11,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Those with healing spells, please get to it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.11,0:19:35.76,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,If any hearts stopped \Nbeating, give them a kick!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.76,0:19:37.16,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Please hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.75,0:19:44.12,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,I can't believe Sitri shoots \Npressurized potion to heal people.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.94,0:19:48.37,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Clever use of a water pistol.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.85,0:19:51.91,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,That idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.32,0:19:57.17,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Sophia told him to take \N{\i1}all{\i0} the Malice Eaters!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.17,0:19:59.11,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Why did he only take one?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.11,0:20:01.04,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Why can he not follow a single command?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.04,0:20:03.94,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Does he still not see the \Ndifference in ability?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.94,0:20:07.81,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,Even with Flick's Calamity Thunder, \Nthe damage to their troop was minimal.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.81,0:20:10.30,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,It seems they keep marching on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.79,0:20:14.00,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,Everything is running counter\N to our expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.00,0:20:17.51,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,The transmogrified phantoms were \Ndefeated, our location was easily deduced,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.51,0:20:19.54,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,and not even Calamity Thunder was effective.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.54,0:20:23.83,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,It's as if Thousand Tricks had engineered \Neverything to turn out like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.86,0:20:26.83,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Those insufferable hunters!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.83,0:20:28.90,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,Sir, you at least need to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.90,0:20:33.59,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,We'll hold them off using \Nthe remaining Malice Eaters.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.86,0:20:35.69,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.69,0:20:38.08,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,We've still got an ace up our sleeves.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.08,0:20:39.40,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,We have Akasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.40,0:20:41.95,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Not to mention, we still have Sophia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.39,0:20:46.92,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,We have no need to abandon this \Nplace until we've completely lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.92,0:20:50.60,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Witnessing my disciples fight to the \Nbitter end is also my responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.60,0:20:52.35,Default,Joe,0,0,0,,Master of Mages!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.35,0:20:53.49,Default,Nole,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.49,0:20:57.35,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,In the name of the Akashic Tower, \Ndestroy the investigation troop!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.35,0:21:00.26,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Go forth and win, my disciples!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.26,0:21:01.10,Default,All,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.01,0:21:04.37,Default,Noctus,0,0,0,,Right, Sophia?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.47,0:21:11.63,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,What a bother.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.63,0:21:16.58,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,There's no doubt. Noctus Cochlear's \Nheadquarters are further into this cave.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.58,0:21:19.58,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,So get through them before \Nthey get us first, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.58,0:21:22.63,Default,Sven,0,0,0,,Just like Krai, you're \Nasking for the impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.85,0:21:25.85,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Not for the former "War Demon," it isn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.50,0:21:31.90,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Sven, Sitri, entrust your lives to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.09,0:21:34.02,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,The three of us will go in first.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.02,0:21:35.42,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,The mages will back us up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.42,0:21:37.23,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,First, we have to cut down the chimeras.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.23,0:21:40.03,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,Then everyone enters to crush them!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.58,0:21:46.06,Default,Gark,0,0,0,,I can't let this end with \NLiz mocking me like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.63,0:21:48.27,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.27,0:21:52.10,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,Looks like traces of some \Nkinda lightning spell.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.79,0:21:55.18,Default,Liz,0,0,0,,A pretty mediocre one, at that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.86,0:22:00.98,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Given the scale of this thing, \NI don't know if "mediocre" is the word...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.92,0:22:04.41,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,The decisive battle is \Nfinally drawing close.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.93,0:22:08.80,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,What is Noctus Cochlear's \Nultimate weapon, "Akasha"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.80,0:22:11.27,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,What will Sophia Black's next move be?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.18,0:22:17.18,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,And will our Krai Andrey continue \Nto not be part of any of this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.45,0:22:18.90,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,Find out in the next episode!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.90,0:22:20.34,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,Please tune in next time!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.70,0:23:31.59,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,All right, everyone! Do your best!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.72,0:23:44.73,EpTitle,Text,0,0,0,,{\fs15\pos(478.445,354.111)}By: Sitri Smart on stage
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.59,0:23:33.00,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,Come on, come on, everyone tough it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.00,0:23:34.56,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,The final battle with Noctus Cochlear!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.56,0:23:35.46,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,Go, go, boom, boom,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.46,0:23:36.17,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.17,0:23:37.67,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,This is it! The moment of truth!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.67,0:23:40.03,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,The Akashic Tower still\Nhas tricks up its sleeve!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.03,0:23:42.18,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,The earth splits, and\Nsomething jet-black appears?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.40,0:23:44.73,Top,Sitri,0,0,0,,Next time on{\i1} Let This Grieving Soul Retire{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.73,0:23:50.02,EpTitle,txt,0,0,0,,{\c&H00BAFF&\pos(320.52,100.623)}Episode 09
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.73,0:23:50.02,EpTitle,txt,0,0,0,,{\fs30\bord3\pos(322.143,238.714)\c&HD1D1D1&}I Want to Teach Love and Peace
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.05,0:23:47.69,Default,Sitri,0,0,0,,Okay, Krai, one for the road?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.69,0:23:49.72,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,"I Want to Teach Love and Peace."
